WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:01.890
Love.

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:07.020
Love is more beautiful, more noble,
and a more diligent worker than anyone else.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.230
It must be...

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.900
...the day you tell the ones
you love how you feel...

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.700
We call it "Valentine's Day"!

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:17.990
<i>Death!</i>

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:48.580
"Episode 5: Work Hard! Valentine's Day"

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.540
Valentine's Day?

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:53.340
Indeed. Valentine's Day.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.380
It's a tradition in Kazuma's world

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.630
where you give chocolate to the one you love.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.510
Chocolate, huh?

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:06.930
I love chocolate, so it feels like
a waste to give it to somebody else.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:10.100
Who will you be giving this "chocolate" to?

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.770
Kazuma, I suppose.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.900
That was a fast answer.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.990
He's never really experienced
Valentine's Day in his life, it seems.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:20.660
He was saying his mom was
the only one to ever give him chocolate.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.120
By the way, do you have someone
to give chocolate to, Emilia?

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:27.120
Puck, maybe?

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.040
Yay! I'll give you some, too.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.290
Thanks, Puck!

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:35.300
I don't think that's how it works...

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.460
Oh, Major!

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.590
Oh, what's going on, everyone?

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:45.220
We were just talking about Valentine's Day.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.270
Valentine's Day?

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.730
That's a story of the victory
of the marketplace,

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.560
and how capitalism was able to successfully
wrest control away from religion.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.610
That's an amazing way to put it.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:59.240
Are you giving chocolate to anyone?

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.610
Personally, I'd much rather not.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:07.080
But if I can get it paid for out of
the expense budget, I could do it.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.620
Duty chocolate, they call it.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.500
Duty chocolate?

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:17.960
Yeah. You give it to people at your work or
to your friends as a way of saying thank you.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.130
You have to give out a lot of chocolate, huh?

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.300
Don't worry.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.140
It can be cheap and small.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.300
It doesn't have to be expensive.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.600
That's good.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:30.230
I need to give Subaru some
"duty chocolate," too.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.690
That's smart thinking, Lia.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.520
Sucks to be Subaru, huh?

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.150
Yeah.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:37.610
"Home Ec Room"

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.070
Valentine's Day!

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:46.120
It's time for the only holiday those foolish
humans celebrate that I approve of!

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:50.200
I'll put all my love, my love!
Into these sweet squares...

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.290
That's right!

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.040
Put your love! Love! Love! Love!

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.250
Into the chocolate!

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.500
Of course, Mr. Betelgeuse!

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.300
Excellent.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.470
I am Betelgeuse Romanée-Conti,
the servant of diligent love.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:05.840
"Love"

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.140
<i>Death!</i>

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.600
Now...

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.850
There are any number of ways to make chocolate.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:17.060
What would you like to make?

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:22.070
Hmm... Lord Ains is the ruler of all the dead!

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:26.070
I want to give him dark, black, bitter
chocolate to match his dark nature!

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:30.240
So instead of sweet,
you prefer an adult bitterness?

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.830
Chocolate covered in my love for him!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.330
And the secret ingredient is my...

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.790
...love!

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.500
Wonderful! Wonderful!

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:43.050
I'm so pleased to have found
someone as diligent as you!

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:47.090
I cannot allow sloth to stand
between me and Lord Ains!

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:51.930
You are truly, truly, truly, truly
a diligent apostle of love!

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:55.480
Yes! I am Lord Ains' love slave!

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.980
<i>Death!</i>

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:04.570
Meanwhile, Kazuma was thinking, "I need to
stay the hell away from these weirdos."

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.530
"Nurse's Office"

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.200
Who will you be giving chocolate to?

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.660
Lord Ains, of course!

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.000
Subaru, for me!

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.620
You're not going to give any to Kazuma?

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.130
Kazuma?

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.630
You're not?

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.840
Kazuma's just a fellow party member.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.010
You're sure?

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:26.260
Of course not!

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:27.760
He's the kind of guy who,

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.800
when we're having a sword fight,
uses magic to soak me in water,

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.180
exposing my naughtiness to the world,

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.140
and then steals away my
strength and licks his lips

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.980
while promising to do unspeakable things to me!

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.600
That sounds like something you'd like.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:43.150
I want chocolate!

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.860
The chocolate is like...

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:46.780
How to say it?

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.740
Really good!

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:52.120
I can't even remember what chocolate
in our last world tasted like anymore!

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.410
--Captain Weiss.
--And today's the only day of the year
when girls give you chocolate!

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:58.170
--And today's the only day of the year
when girls give you chocolate!

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.040
Captain Weiss.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:02.090
Is it okay for us to have such a happy day?

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:03.500
Captain Weiss!

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:04.800
What?

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:08.130
That's not how today works.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:12.800
Today, girls give chocolate to people they like.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:15.680
So you get chocolate and the girl likes you!

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.180
Even better!

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.190
Yeah, this is no good.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.190
He doesn't get it.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:20.020
Right?

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.810
It's not right, Neumann!

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:25.110
Explain how this works to this bozo.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.440
Leave it to me.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.030
Captain Weiss.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.370
That's right.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:35.990
Today you get to ask girls for chocolate.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:40.710
But you must be appropriately polite.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:44.590
Well of course.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.420
Hey, Kazuma!

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.670
Neumann! What's up?

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:53.760
When you wanted chocolate from a girl
in your world, what did you say?

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:56.350
Hmm...

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.850
<i>Give me!</i>

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.640
<i>Choco!</i>

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.270
Yeah.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:05.440
Give me choco?

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:09.110
Yes. Offer out your hands and bow politely,

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:12.530
then keep asking, and you can
get all the chocolate you want!

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.700
Kazuma! Thank you!

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.910
No need for thanks.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.290
Bye!

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.630
Not a chance in hell that's true.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:24.540
Right?

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.340
It's not right.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:30.380
Look, Captain Weiss is taking it seriously!

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:33.590
Look, here come the girls now!

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:36.430
--That's right.
--Great idea!

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:43.270
<i>Give me... choco!</i>

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:45.810
What the hell?

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:51.530
<i>Give me... choco!</i>

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.240
Hold it right there, strong eyebrows!

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:55.450
If you want to attack someone, attack me!

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:59.160
<i>Give me... choco!</i>

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.080
Al Huma!

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.830
Let's go.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.590
Yes, let's.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:13.220
Why won't anybody give me chocolate?

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:14.050
Right?

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:15.050
It's not right!

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.930
I'm actually feeling bad for Captain Weiss.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.690
What's wrong, Captain Weiss?

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:26.560
You're a mess.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.070
Major...

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:32.070
What? Did something happen?

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.320
Give...

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:39.660
Give me... choco...

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:42.950
Captain Weiss.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:44.210
Yes?

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:47.130
Someone was lying to you.

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:51.920
Splendid.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:54.760
Truly, truly, truly, truly splendid!

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:58.510
Truly love given physical form!

00:08:58.510 --> 00:08:59.640
<i>Death!</i>

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.350
What are you two doing?

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:08.650
I was just making chocolate
for my beloved Lord Ains!

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.070
Diligently! Yes, diligently!

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.690
That's wonderful.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:16.150
And who is this?

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:18.530
A pleasure to make your acquaintance.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:21.030
I am the apostle of diligent love,

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:24.790
Archbishop of the Sin of Sloth,
Betelgeuse Romanée-Conti!

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:25.710
Death!

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:28.380
You're a trespasser, aren't you?

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.540
Death!

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:31.670
Death!

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.760
Death!

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.590
Well, it all worked out.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:41.470
My goal has already been achieved.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:45.310
Oh? I feel something that way, too...

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:47.810
Love! An aura of love!

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:50.360
I must go! Death!

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.480
Thank you, apostle of love.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:55.690
Hey, Albedo.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.490
Making chocolate by yourself.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:58.740
Oh, Subaru.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.870
By the way, what do you think of
this Valentine's Chocolate?

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.790
Will Lord Ains like it?

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.290
Well?

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.630
Love... Don't you think it's filled with love?

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:16.550
To be honest, the design looks
pretty negative to me.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:20.090
But the love looks strong.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.220
Death.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:49.720
But you know...

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:52.110
...I can't eat chocolate.
